Yes. The MCP server uses your account’s [free tier](/general/account/billing-and-pricing/free-tier) of 5,000 credits per month. Web search (SERP API) and web page scraping ([Fetch API](/products/scrapers/fetch-api/introduction)) cost one credit per request.
You can get your API token from the [user settings page](https://brightdata.com/cp/setting/users) in your Bright Data account. Make sure you have an account on [brightdata.com](https://brightdata.com) - new users get free credit for testing, and pay-as-you-go options are available after that.
No. The Bright Data MCP server only requires an API token, for both the remote (hosted) and local (self-hosted) setup. Usernames (format: `brd-customer-{customer_id}-zone-{zone_name}`) are only used for native proxy access and are not needed for MCP, SDK or API integrations.If a third-party tool or integration asks for a username, you can leave it empty or check whether it is actually configuring proxy access.

"mcpServers": {
"Bright Data": {
"command": "/usr/local/bin/node", // Replace with your actual Node.js path
"args": ["node_modules/@brightdata/mcp/index.js"],
"env": {
"API_TOKEN": "YOUR_API_KEY"
}
}

Yes! Every Bright Data account gets **5,000 free credits per month**, and the MCP server draws from them. They cover web search and web page scraping. See What is the MCP free tier? below for more details.
The MCP free tier allows you to connect your AI agent via MCP (Model Context Protocol) to Bright Data services for free. You get up to 5,000 requests per month for web search and for fetching any public web page, at no cost. This is ideal for testing, development, or light usage.The MCP free tier is not a separate grant. It is the same account-level [free tier](/general/account/billing-and-pricing/free-tier) of 5,000 credits per month, drawn from a single shared pool. MCP search runs on the SERP API and page scraping on the [Fetch API](/products/scrapers/fetch-api/introduction), and both are covered by the free credits.For
